      "question": "What are the key elements of the differential diagnosis?",
      "my_answer": "Differential includes otitis media, otomycosis, foreign body in the ear, and early perichondritis.",
      "rationale": "Otitis media may cause ear pain but typically lacks tragal tenderness and shows bulging tympanic membrane. Otomycosis (fungal infection) can present with debris and itching but often has characteristic hyphae or spores. Foreign body could cause irritation but is less likely without history. Perichondritis involves the auricle cartilage and would show swelling/redness of the pinna, which is absent here."
