      "my_answer": "No red flags are currently present.",
      "rationale": "Absence of fever, cranial nerve deficits (especially facial nerve), mastoid tenderness, periauricular swelling, or immunocompromised state suggests no extension into deeper tissues or skull base (e.g., malignant otitis externa). Pain with chewing may suggest temporomandibular joint referral, but tragal tenderness localizes the pain to the ear canal."
