      "question": "What are the key differential diagnoses to consider?",
      "my_answer": "Cervical radiculopathy (C6-C7), pronator teres syndrome, peripheral neuropathy (e.g., diabetic or hypothyroid), and brachial plexopathy",
      "rationale": "These conditions can mimic CTS. Cervical radiculopathy may present with similar dermatomal symptoms but usually includes neck pain and reflex changes. Pronator teres syndrome involves more proximal median nerve compression. Hypothyroidism is a risk factor for CTS but can also cause generalized neuropathy."
