      "my_answer": "Dix-Hallpike maneuver",
      "rationale": "The Dix-Hallpike test is the gold standard for diagnosing BPPV. It can elicit characteristic nystagmus and reproduce symptoms when the affected ear is positioned downward, confirming canalithiasis in the posterior semicircular canal."
